 400:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_posif.h ****  * De-asserts the POSIF module from reset and enables the clock.\n
 401:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_posif.h ****  * Configures \a PRCLR0 register's \a POSIF0RS or \a POSIF1RS bit field depends upon \a peripheral.
 402:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_posif.h ****  * If running on other than XMC45 device then it will ungate the peripheral clock.
 403:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_posif.h ****  *
 404:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_posif.h ****  * \par<b>Note</b><br>
 405:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_posif.h ****  * This is the first API which application must invoke to configure POSIF.
 406:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_posif.h ****  * It is internally called by XMC_POSIF_Init().
 407:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_posif.h ****  *
 408:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_posif.h ****  * \par<b>Related APIs:</b><BR>
 409:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_posif.h ****  * XMC_POSIF_Disable(),XMC_POSIF_Init() \n\n\n
 410:D:/SoftWar_Debug/XMC1300_GPIO/Libraries/XMCLib/inc\xmc_posif.h ****  */
